stateDiagram-v2
  direction TB
  [*] --> Source

  state "Own-source state" as Source {
    direction TB
    [*] --> Unknown
    Unknown --> Fresh : new admitted sample, age at most 2000 ms
    Unknown --> Stale : admitted sample already over 2000 ms
    Unknown --> Invalid : source admission fails
    Unknown --> Unsupported : unsupported source scope
    Fresh --> Fresh : new admitted current-epoch sample, age at most 2000 ms
    Fresh --> Stale : age exceeds 2000 ms without new observation
    Fresh --> Invalid : admission fails / withdraw live values
    Fresh --> Unsupported : source scope becomes unsupported
    Stale --> Invalid : admission fails
    Stale --> Unsupported : source scope becomes unsupported
    Stale --> Fresh : new admitted sample, age at most 2000 ms
    Invalid --> Fresh : new admitted sample, age at most 2000 ms
    Unsupported --> Fresh : support validated and new admitted fresh sample
  }

  Source --> Source : source generation or confirmed session boundary / fence and reset values

  note right of Fresh
    Age 2000 ms may be fresh; 2001 ms is stale.
    Polling and invalid input never renew source age.
    Late old-generation callbacks are discarded.
  end note
  note right of Invalid
    Withdraw own live values and peer publication.
    Unknown or invalid is not numeric zero.
    Retain verified match identity and watermark
    until actual boundary evidence.
  end note
  note right of Source
    Freshness and match lifecycle are independent.
    A source reset alone does not create a new match.
    Historical values may be labelled stale.
  end note

